    "prompt": "Use case: terrain atlas. Paint18 new natural WALL TOP textures for Mindustry, bright clean refined Daoist Q hand-painted geology guided by attached references' craftsmanship ONLY. Strict directly overhead orthographic, NO UI/text/symbols/people/perspective. Requested1536×3072 portrait. EXACTLY3 EQUAL columns ×6 EQUAL rows, each square fullbleed cell fills edge to edge with opaque natural rock cap, no gutters/borders/labels. Do not make last row or column larger. Every row has2 different small wall variants at left/middle and1 independent larger wall design at right with more crown/fracture details, not copied. Pronounced rounded broad rocky crowns, soft internal shadow cracks, material fills square continuously with quiet tileable edges. Even overhead lighting, no vignette/gradient.\nRow1 BERYLLIC STONE WALL: pale sage-jade gray stone crowns with small green mineral flecks.\nRow2 CARBON WALL: dark blue charcoal carbon-rich rock crowns, rounded large smooth plates and deep soft cracks, no lava.\nRow3 FERRIC STONE WALL: muted warm iron-brown ocher rock crowns with small rusty orange flecks.\nRow4 RHYOLITE WALL: muted lavender-gray volcanic rock crowns, subtle fine layered streaks, few small pebbles between crowns.\nRow5 REGOLITH WALL: pale mauve-tan compact moonrock crowns with tiny soft pits and powdery texture.\nRow6 YELLOW STONE WALL: warm golden ochre stone crowns with gentle pale beige veins and broad round erosion surfaces.\nRefined painterly coherent material shapes distinct in all18tiles, no architectural brick patterns or isolated object backgrounds.",
